{"id":"6b70445a785741dd24a8744c787d876efdb4ff43","axis":"silent","repo":"phan/phan","sha":"6b70445a785741dd24a8744c787d876efdb4ff43","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"NEWS.md","lines":["@@ -7,6 +7,9 @@ New features:"," - Support PHPStan/Psalm-style conditional return types in `@return`, `@psalm-return` and `@phan-return`, e.g. `@return ($method is null ? HigherOrderMessage : VerificationDirector)` (used by Mockery, guzzle/promises, etc.). The branch is chosen per call site from the argument's type (`is`/`is not`, nesting in either branch, omitted arguments use the parameter's default), falling back to the union of all branches when the argument type is ambiguous. Previously these annotations were rejected with `PhanUnextractableAnnotation` and the method's return type was empty. Implementing methods without their own `@return` inherit the conditional. Adds `PhanCommentReturnConditionalWithoutRealParam` for conditions on a parameter the function doesn't declare. Conditions on template type names (`T is int`) and multi-line conditionals are not supported yet ([#5574](https://github.com/phan/phan/issues/5574))"," - Add `--dump-phase-timings` (text report on stderr) and `--phase-timings-json <path>` (JSON report) to measure the wall clock time, CPU time and memory of each phase of a run (config, parse, class/function/method analysis, ordering, fork, waiting on workers, etc.) and of each analysis worker, along with per-file parse/analysis time percentiles and the slowest files, worker load imbalance, the serial fraction of the run, child teardown time and counts of declared vs. inherited methods. `$GLOBALS['__phase']` is set to the current phase so that sampling profilers such as phpspy can attribute samples to phases. Collection is off by default and does not change analysis results."," ","+Performance improvements:","+- Reduce analysis overhead without changing the emitted issues: FQSEN and `Type` memoization no longer allocate a closure per lookup, `FullyQualifiedClassName::fromType()` is cached per type, `UnionType` string conversion and equality checks are faster for small type sets, whether a file is excluded from analysis is cached per path (and issues in excluded files are no longer formatted before being discarded), the `clone` AST normalization pass is skipped for files that do not contain `clone`, and redundant `realpath()`/stat calls were removed.","+"," Bug fixes:"," - Analysis workers of `--processes N` now terminate without running PHP's shutdown sequence once they have sent their results to the parent (by exec'ing `/bin/true`). Destroying the inherited heap wrote to every object, which copied the copy-on-write pages shared with the parent and the other workers (several GB per worker on large projects) and delayed the parent's output by seconds. Set `PHAN_DISABLE_FAST_EXIT=1` to keep the regular `exit()`; it is also kept when the profiler, xdebug or pcov is active. Analysis results are unchanged."," - Make the output of `--processes N` deterministic: the issues reported by the analysis workers are now combined in worker order instead of the order in which the workers happened to finish. When several workers emit an issue with the same file, line, type and message but different suggestions (e.g. plugins whose `finalizeProcess()` runs in every worker, such as `UnknownElementTypePlugin`'s \"Types inferred after analysis\" suggestion), the same one is now kept on every run instead of whichever worker's results arrived last."],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/AST/Parser.php","lines":["@@ -167,7 +167,10 @@ private static function parseCodeHandlingDeprecation(CodeBase $code_base, Contex","             }","             // Normalize AST to handle differences between PHP versions","             // (e.g., AST 120+ represents 'clone' as AST_CALL instead of AST_CLONE)","-            ASTNormalizer::normalizeCloneNodes($root_node);","+            // php-ast only creates that call for the (case-insensitive) clone keyword, so skip walking the AST when it's absent.","+            if (\\stripos($file_contents, 'clone') !== false) {","+                ASTNormalizer::normalizeCloneNodes($root_node);","+            }","             return $root_node;","         } finally {","             $__no_echo_phan_errors = false;","@@ -440,7 +443,10 @@ public static function parseCodePolyfill(CodeBase $code_base, Context $context,","         if (!$errors) {","             // Normalize AST to handle differences between PHP versions","             // (e.g., AST 120+ represents 'clone' as AST_CALL instead of AST_CLONE)","-            ASTNormalizer::normalizeCloneNodes($node);","+            // (skipped when the source can't contain the clone keyword)","+            if (\\stripos($file_contents, 'clone') !== false) {","+                ASTNormalizer::normalizeCloneNodes($node);","+            }","             return $node;","         }","         $file_position_map = new FilePositionMap($file_contents);","@@ -483,7 +489,10 @@ public static function parseCodePolyfill(CodeBase $code_base, Context $context,","         }","         // Normalize AST to handle differences between PHP versions","         // (e.g., AST 120+ represents 'clone' as AST_CALL instead of AST_CLONE)","-        ASTNormalizer::normalizeCloneNodes($node);","+        // (skipped when the source can't contain the clone keyword)","+        if (\\stripos($file_contents, 'clone') !== false) {","+            ASTNormalizer::normalizeCloneNodes($node);","+        }","         return $node;","     }"," "],"additions":12,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Analysis/ArgumentType.php","lines":["@@ -1178,16 +1178,20 @@ public static function analyzeParameter(CodeBase $code_base, Context $context, F","         $alternate_parameter_type = null;  // TODO: Properly merge \"possibly undefined\" union types - without this, undefined is inferred instead of possibly undefined"," ","         // Check ArrayObject and ArrayIterator","-        // @phan-suppress-next-line PhanThrowTypeAbsentForCall","-        $arrayObj = FullyQualifiedClassName::make('', 'ArrayObject');","-        // @phan-suppress-next-line PhanThrowTypeAbsentForCall","-        $arrayIter = FullyQualifiedClassName::make('', 'ArrayIterator');","-        $deprecatedParam = false;","-        if ($method->getFQSEN() === FullyQualifiedMethodName::make($arrayObj, '__construct')","-            || $method->getFQSEN() === FullyQualifiedMethodName::make($arrayIter, '__construct')","-        ) {","-            $deprecatedParam = true;","-        }","+        // (The FQSEN factories always return the same instances, so these are only created once)","+        static $array_object_constructor_fqsen = null;","+        static $array_iterator_constructor_fqsen = null;","+        if ($array_object_constructor_fqsen === null) {","+            // @phan-suppress-next-line PhanThrowTypeAbsentForCall","+            $arrayObj = FullyQualifiedClassName::make('', 'ArrayObject');","+            // @phan-suppress-next-line PhanThrowTypeAbsentForCall","+            $arrayIter = FullyQualifiedClassName::make('', 'ArrayIterator');","+            $array_object_constructor_fqsen = FullyQualifiedMethodName::make($arrayObj, '__construct');","+            $array_iterator_constructor_fqsen = FullyQualifiedMethodName::make($arrayIter, '__construct');","+        }","+        $method_fqsen = $method->getFQSEN();","+        $deprecatedParam = $method_fqsen === $array_object_constructor_fqsen","+            || $method_fqsen === $array_iterator_constructor_fqsen;"," ","         $arg_count_info = null;","         foreach ($method->alternateGenerator($code_base) as $alternate_method) {"],"additions":14,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Analysis/PreOrderAnalysisVisitor.php","lines":["@@ -120,8 +120,10 @@ public function visitClass(Node $node): Context","             $clazz = $this->code_base->getClassByFQSEN(","                 $class_fqsen","           